      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, u mentioned 'progressive planning' as the trend... but isn't the argument for keeping single-family zones actually quite practical? people move there specifically for the stability and the schools, and it protects their biggest investment. seems like a lot of people just call it 'NIMBYism' to dismiss it, but aren't there legitimate reasons why people want to keep their neighborhoods the way they are?",
